# Build context filter for the root Dockerfile.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# The repo root carries ~1.7 MB of docs/tree dumps, a ~900 KB pair of committed
# SQLite files under backend/, a Windows virtualenv, and a full node_modules
# tree. Without this file every one of them is uploaded to the Docker daemon on
# every build and most of them land in the image — slow builds, a fat image, and
# (for .env and the .db files) real data inside a shipped artefact.
#
# Rule of thumb: the image contains only what `python -m uvicorn main:app` needs
# to serve a request. Everything else is developer or repository furniture.
#
# NOTE: this file governs builds that use the REPO ROOT as context (the backend
# image). The commented-out frontend service in docker-compose.yml builds with
# ./frontend as its context, so it reads frontend/.dockerignore instead and is
# unaffected by the `frontend/` exclusion below.

# ── Version control and CI ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.gitignore.txt
.github
.claude

# ── Virtualenvs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# backend/venv is a *Windows* venv on the dev machine. Copying it in would both
# bloat the image and shadow the Linux site-packages pip installs below it.
venv/
.venv/
**/venv/
**/.venv/

# ── Python bytecode ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The dev .env points DATABASE_URL at localhost, which would be wrong inside a
# container anyway — but the real reason is that credentials must never be baked
# into an image layer. Config arrives as environment variables at run time.
# .env.example is excluded too: it is documentation, and documentation lives in
# the repo, not in the runtime image.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*

# ── Tests ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately NOT in the production image. The `tests` service in
# docker-compose.yml bind-mounts ./backend over /app so the suites are present
# when — and only when — you are running them. Keeping them out means the
# shipped image cannot be talked into executing test code.
**/test_*.py
**/*_test.py
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/conftest.py

# ── Local databases ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# backend/ci.db and backend/flowmes.db are committed SQLite files. Production is
# Postgres; shipping a stale SQLite snapshot is exactly the confusion this whole
# change set is trying to end.
*.db
*.sqlite3
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite3

# ── Documentation and repository furniture ──────────────────────────────
# (backend/modules.json is NOT documentation — module_manifest.py reads it at
# import time to build the plan gate, so it must stay in the image. It is a
# .json and none of the patterns here touch it.)
docs/
*.md
tree.txt
privacy-policy.html
generate_pdf.py
*.pdf
FlowMES-Enterprise/

# ── Historical SQL migrations ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The application does not read these at run time — the boot path in main.py
# applies its own idempotent Python migrations. They are kept in the repo as
# history; they have no business in the image.
backend/migration_*.sql

# ── Frontend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The backend image serves an API only. node_modules alone is larger than
# everything else in this repo combined.
frontend/

# ── Editor / OS noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
